   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "",
      "body": "<h3>Tools should be used to balance them. Balancing helps you better manage risks—at any speed.</h3>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c705",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "",
      "body": "<p><strong>Many precision grinders and machinists associate balancing exclusively with very high rotational speeds. In fact, however, every rotating tool has the potential for unbalance. The negative consequences can be immediate—or they can trigger high costs and machine downtime only after some time has passed. </strong></p> <p>Balancing leads to greater cost-effectiveness because it reduces cost-driving tool wear. It prevents expensive machine downtime and minimizes time-consuming quality complaints. <br/>ZOLLER’s toolBalancer series features balancing technology that is unique worldwide. The newly developed devices offer many innovations that elevate precision, safety, ergonomics, and operation to an unprecedented level of quality.</p> <p>Minimize manufacturing risks. With ZOLLER—the most advanced balancing technology on the market. </p> <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/ca/products/tool-balancing-technology/toolbalancer\">Display products</a></p>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c706",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ]
   ],
   "ftype": "container-2cols",
   "id": "c704",
   "bg": "",
   "space": {
    "before": "extra-small",
    "after": "default"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h2> Exact Measurement with a High Sensor Signal </h2>",
   "body": "<p>A distinctive feature of every »toolBalancer« is its measurement method. ZOLLER uses a specialized balance adapter with a center offset, two-point contact, and a pressure pad.</p> <p>This measuring technology approach amplifies the sensor signal and thus improves the quality of the measurement. You’ll get exceptionally accurate balancing results. </p>",
   "images": [],
   "videos": [],
   "pos": "text",
   "cols": 1,
   "valign": "center",
   "ftype": "textmedia",
   "id": "c707",
   "bg": "black",
   "space": {
    "before": "extra-large",
    "after": "extra-large"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h2 class=\"headline-decor\"> Restore the peace </h2>",
   "body": "<p class=\"large-text\">Maximize smooth operation with balanced tools. They reduce centrifugal forces in the drives of your CNC machines, avoid unnecessary maintenance, and protect against spindle damage.</p> <p class=\"large-text\">With balancing results of &lt; 0.4 gmm, ZOLLER’s Tool Balancing Technology provides additional protection for the productivity of your machines. »toolBalancer« identifies even low unbalances that can place heavy strain on spindles or bearings and shorten the service life of components. </p>",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/1/8/csm_balancing_01_4186f932b3.webp",
     "alt": "",
     "w": 1920,
     "h": 1967
    }
   ],
   "videos": [],
   "pos": "right",
   "cols": 1,
   "valign": "center",
   "ftype": "textmedia",
   "id": "c708",
   "bg": "white",
   "space": {
    "before": "small",
    "after": "small"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h2 class=\"headline-decor\"> Greater stability during tool life </h2>",
   "body": "<p class=\"large-text\">Regular balancing using ZOLLER’s precision technology keeps tool life consistently high. You’ll enjoy long-term benefits from greater cost-effectiveness and a rapid return on your investment. </p> <p class=\"large-text\">If a rotating tool runs even slightly out of round, additional forces act on the cutting edge. Tool life decreases, tool costs rise, and tool change intervals become shorter. </p>",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/7/7/csm_balancing_02_aaf3ff5460.webp",
     "alt": "",
     "w": 1220,
     "h": 1250
    }
   ],
   "videos": [],
   "pos": "right",
   "cols": 1,
   "valign": "center",
   "ftype": "textmedia",
   "id": "c709",
   "bg": "white",
   "space": {
    "before": "none",
    "after": "none"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h2 class=\"headline-decor\"> Top-quality surfaces </h2>",
   "body": "<p class=\"large-text\">Eliminate unbalances in tools and grinding wheels as a risk that compromises quality. ZOLLER’s Tool Balancing Technology simplifies the process of achieving surfaces that meet the standards of even the most demanding industries.</p> <p class=\"large-text\">If tools run out of round, it can lead to surface quality defects. Usually, cutting parameters or the tool itself are suspected as the cause. However, by the time an unbalance is considered, a significant amount of machine uptime, material, and tool life has already been wasted. </p>",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/d/8/csm_balancing_03_8d69d2b1ea.webp",
     "alt": "",
     "w": 1920,
     "h": 1967
    }
